Content lines are now unfolded on the raw bytes before decoding, so a fold
point can no longer split a multi-byte UTF-8 character (e.g. Chinese text
or emoji in ``DESCRIPTION``) into orphaned continuation bytes. Illegal
folding, bare carriage returns, unclosed quotation marks, and invalid
UTF-8 now raise :class:`~icalendar.error.ParseError` with the offset of
the problem in strict mode, while the lenient default keeps its existing
tolerance. Parameter parsing distinguishes quoted and unquoted tokens, and
the backslash escaping of property values stays separate from the quoting
of parameter values.
